1
00:00:00,368 --> 00:00:04,243
Before asking Copilot to edit, open
Source Control in the training

2
00:00:04,293 --> 00:00:05,493
workspace.

3
00:00:05,543 --> 00:00:09,387
The demonstration starts on a disposable
branch with a clean working tree.

4
00:00:10,011 --> 00:00:13,731
If you already have edits, note their
files and contents.

5
00:00:13,806 --> 00:00:15,831
That baseline matters later.

6
00:00:15,906 --> 00:00:19,381
You want to recognize your own work
before using a control that can discard

7
00:00:19,406 --> 00:00:20,049
a change.

8
00:00:21,606 --> 00:00:23,406
Look at the proposed patch.

9
00:00:23,481 --> 00:00:28,081
One change replaces greater than or
equal to zero with greater than zero.

10
00:00:28,131 --> 00:00:30,554
The new assertion checks the missing
boundary case.

11
00:00:31,188 --> 00:00:33,638
A third change touches a notes file.

12
00:00:33,713 --> 00:00:37,288
Read that diff and ask which requirement
it satisfies.

13
00:00:37,363 --> 00:00:41,438
In this exercise it is unrelated, so we
can remove it while keeping the two

14
00:00:41,488 --> 00:00:42,379
useful edits.

15
00:00:43,851 --> 00:00:46,676
Review the runner output linked to the
exercise.

16
00:00:46,726 --> 00:00:50,201
Before the source edit, the zero
assertion failed for the expected

17
00:00:50,251 --> 00:00:51,151
reason.

18
00:00:51,226 --> 00:00:54,236
After the edit, it passes with three
earlier cases.

19
00:00:54,849 --> 00:00:58,324
Keep both outputs visible while
evaluating the patch.

20
00:00:58,374 --> 00:01:02,199
They help explain why the validator and
test edits belong together and the

21
00:01:02,249 --> 00:01:03,843
unrelated note does not.

22
00:01:05,310 --> 00:01:07,760
Open the notes diff in Source Control.

23
00:01:07,835 --> 00:01:12,789
If the file contains only the unwanted
agent edit, discard that file's change.

24
00:01:13,403 --> 00:01:17,778
If it also contains work you need, use a
narrower edit or revert the confirmed

25
00:01:17,828 --> 00:01:18,703
hunk.

26
00:01:18,778 --> 00:01:20,477
Read the diff again after the action.

27
00:01:21,076 --> 00:01:24,975
The validator and the added test should
still be in the changed-file list.

28
00:01:26,476 --> 00:01:28,451
Check Source Control again.

29
00:01:28,526 --> 00:01:33,401
Confirm the validator and test are the
only changes expected for this exercise,

30
00:01:33,451 --> 00:01:35,918
then rerun the suite in the approved
environment.

31
00:01:36,555 --> 00:01:38,380
All four tests should pass.

32
00:01:38,455 --> 00:01:42,755
If the regression disappears from the
run, inspect the test diff again.

33
00:01:42,830 --> 00:01:46,630
Verifying the result after undo is what
tells you that the useful changes

34
00:01:46,680 --> 00:01:47,274
survived.

35
00:01:48,764 --> 00:01:51,639
When one hunk is wrong, reverse that
hunk.

36
00:01:51,714 --> 00:01:54,564
If a whole file contains just the
unwanted edit,

37
00:01:54,614 --> 00:01:56,546
a file-level discard may be enough.

38
00:01:57,160 --> 00:02:00,960
For a broader session checkpoint, read
which changes it will affect before

39
00:02:01,010 --> 00:02:02,185
using it.

40
00:02:02,235 --> 00:02:06,110
The choice depends on the diff you
inspected and any unrelated work that

41
00:02:06,160 --> 00:02:07,263
must stay in place.

42
00:02:08,772 --> 00:02:11,197
Finish by explaining the final patch.

43
00:02:11,297 --> 00:02:13,072
Zero is now rejected.

44
00:02:13,122 --> 00:02:15,097
The signature stays the same.

45
00:02:15,147 --> 00:02:18,637
The new test proves the boundary, and
the original cases still pass.

46
00:02:19,265 --> 00:02:23,415
Name the unrelated edit you removed and
show the remaining diff.

47
00:02:23,490 --> 00:02:27,340
That gives your teammate both the change
they need to review and the evidence you

48
00:02:27,390 --> 00:02:28,660
checked after recovery.
